# Transaction boundaries

Spring `@Transactional` only applies across a **different bean**. When to add an
internal service: see `service-layers.mdc`.

- Do not call `this.someTransactionalMethod()` — self-invocation skips the proxy.
- Do not put `@Transactional` on a private method.
- Do not run outbound I/O (S3, HTTP, queues) inside a `@Transactional` method or
  between two statements of the same transaction.
- Best-effort I/O (cleanup) catches and logs its own exceptions; it must not roll
  back the caller.
- `Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW` only when that write must survive a parent rollback;
  document why on the method.

Mixed I/O + DB (contracted impl not `@Transactional`; JDBC on internal):

```java
String publicUrl = storageService.moveToPublicBucket(key); // I/O first
profileRecordService.updateImageUrl(profileId, publicUrl); // other bean, @Transactional
storageService.cleanupLandingZone(key); // best-effort I/O
```
